DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The rriippccttll program controls the ripd(8) daemon.  Commands may be abbrevi‐
     ated to the minimum unambiguous prefix; for example, ss nn for sshhooww
     nneeiigghhbboorr.

     The following options are available:

     --ss _s_o_c_k_e_t
             Use _s_o_c_k_e_t instead of the default _/_v_a_r_/_r_u_n_/_r_i_p_d_._s_o_c_k to communi‐
             cate with ripd(8).

     The following commands are available:

     ffiibb ccoouuppllee
             Insert the learned routes into the Forward Information Base
             a.k.a. the kernel routing table.

     ffiibb ddeeccoouuppllee
             Remove the learned routes from the Forward Information Base
             a.k.a. the kernel routing table.  Decoupling the FIB from an RIP
             router may create routing loops and could cause major routing is‐
             sues.

     lloogg bbrriieeff
             Disable verbose debug logging.

     lloogg vveerrbboossee
             Enable verbose debug logging.

     sshhooww ffiibb [_d_e_s_t_i_n_a_t_i_o_n | _f_i_l_t_e_r]
             Show the Forwarding Information Base.  _d_e_s_t_i_n_a_t_i_o_n can be speci‐
             fied to show the route matching a destination IP address.  _f_i_l_t_e_r
             can be any of the following:

             ccoonnnneecctteedd               Show only connected routes.
             iinntteerrffaaccee               Show only interfaces.
             rriipp                     Show only RIP routes.
             ssttaattiicc                  Show only static routes.

             ccoonnnneecctteedd, rriipp, and ssttaattiicc may be specified together.

     sshhooww iinntteerrffaacceess
             Show details for all interfaces.

     sshhooww nneeiigghhbboorr
             Show neighbors.

     sshhooww rriibb
             Show the Routing Information Base.

